--- tutorial/checkpoints/05-goblin/README.md
+++ tutorial/checkpoints/06-archery/README.md
@@ -1 +1 @@
-# 05 — A turn now has consequences
+# 06 — The archer earns the name
@@ -5,2 +5 @@
-Checkpoint 04 has meaningful walls and an exit, but the room is safe and the
-shortest path is automatic.
+Checkpoint 05 adds pressure and fair warning, but the only response is to run.
@@ -10,2 +9,2 @@
-Without pressure there is no reason to weigh one movement against another. A
-single pursuer makes the turn model visible before combat adds another action.
+An archer should trade a scarce resource for safety. The existing map already
+makes direction and line of sight meaningful.
@@ -15,4 +14,4 @@
-A goblin takes one response after each effective player turn. First adjacency
-only warns. If the player begins the next action adjacent and fails to escape,
-the goblin deals one HP; safe no-ops remain free. `TurnResult` carries player
-and enemy events so rules are observable instead of inferred by the CLI.
+I/J/K/L shoots up/left/down/right. A shot consumes one of three arrows, walks
+cell by cell until a wall, and kills the goblin if the line crosses it. Hit,
+miss, and empty-quiver outcomes are distinct; twin control diamonds make both
+directional action families visible.
